Change: Build Roc's interpreter shim as a wasm32-freestanding archive for the
Tour host. The shim compiles out the ipc module (it needs mmap and an OS) and
takes its memory from the host's memalign and free, because emscripten owns
memory.grow. It adds the tour-shim-wasm32-freestanding build step.
Upstream: not proposed. A general "shim for wasm hosts" change could go
upstream; ask on the Roc Zulip first.
Source: research/tour-interpreter-in-tour-host (build-zig.patch, items 1 and 2
of interpreter-shim.patch).

